the\0aapproval ledger: the moment a claim activates (eng review blocker\0a#2: the mandatory 7-day cooldown must never count as staker\0ainactivity). Updated to `now` on every successful `claim_stream`.\0aChecked by the permissionless `expire_stale_claim`. Unused (0)\0abefore activation.\00\00\00\00\00\00\15last_collected_ledger\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00qStake amount captured at submit_claim, used by cancel_claim to\0arestore total_staked on a false-positive reversal.\00\00\00\00\00\00\05stake\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06status\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bClaimStatus\00\00\00\00+Already streamed to the beneficiary so far.\00\00\00\00\08streamed\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00oAssessed by the oracle at claim time, included in its signed\0averdict: never re-derivable/forgeable client-side.\00\00\00\00\04tier\00\00\00\04\00\00\02\feCORRECTED 2026-07-14 (second pass, full source read): NOT \22fixed at\0aend of cooldown\22 as an earlier note claimed. Activation happens\0asynchronously: either inside submit_claim itself (gate already\0amet) or inside unlock_pending_claim (gate met later), and\0acooldown_ends/vesting_ends are set as FUTURE deadlines starting\0afrom that same activation moment, not preconditions for it. The\0asnapshot is total_staked read immediately before THIS claim's own\0aforfeiture decrement, in that same call. Still matters for the\0asame reason: get the timing wrong and the outflow cap's\0aanti-manipulation guarantee breaks.\0av1 (2026-09-22): now snapshots CAPACITY (`total_staked +\0atotal_backed`), not staker principal alone. Field name kept: struct\0afield names are part of the stored XDR.\00\00\00\00\00\15total_staked_snapshot\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07tx_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13vesting_ends_ledger\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06wallet\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bClaimStatus\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Unused\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Active\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Completed\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Cancelled\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08Reserved\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bPendingTime\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\01\13NEW 2026-07-22 (Rule A): 90-day gate met, reservation live, nothing\0aforfeited yet: waiting on the staker's own `approve_claim` call\0awithin `APPROVE_WINDOW_LEDGERS`. Replaces the old behavior where\0ameeting the time gate auto-forfeited the stake with no staker\0aaction required.\00\00\00\00\10AwaitingApproval\00\00\00\06\00\00\01\b6NEW 2026-07-22: terminal state for a reservation that lapsed\0awithout staker action: either Rule A (never approved in time) or\0aRule B (approved, then went inactive too long during collection).\0aSame downstream handling either way: release whatever's still\0areserved, stop further action. Distinct from `Cancelled`, which\0aimplies an admin false-positive judgment call and its associated\0apenalty-lock logic: an expiry is neither party's fault.\00\00\00\00\00\07Expired\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bStakeRecord\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\01\fcCHANGED 2026-07-22 (eng review, bug 2 fix): was a bare `claim_active:\0abool`. A bool alone can't distinguish \22re-executing/correcting THIS\0aSAME claim\22 from \22wallet already has a DIFFERENT claim in flight\22,\0a`execute_override` needs that distinction to enforce the one-wallet-\0aone-claim invariant, which a bool structurally cannot express.\0a`Some(claim_id)` while any claim is open against this stake (blocks\0awithdrawal, same as the old bool); `None` once terminal\0a(Completed/Cancelled/Expired) or never claimed.\00\00\00\0factive_claim_id\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\f0sha256(beneficiary), plaintext beneficiary address is never stored.\0aDecided 2026-07-14: sha256 not keccak256 (Soroban-native, consistent\0awith the Ed25519 oracle-auth decision; no cross-chain hash-matching\0arequirement exists for this field).\00\00\00\10beneficiary_hash\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\c8Pre-audit hardening (2026-09-23): set when a claim on this stake is\0aapproved (the stake is forfeited). The address can never stake again\0a(pool rule). Cleared only by `cancel_claim` undoing that claim.\00\00\00\0eclaim_approved\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00qSet by cancel_claim on a false-positive reversal; blocks withdraw\0afor PENALTY_LOCK_LEDGERS. 0 if never penalized.\00\00\00\00\00\00\1bpenalty_locked_until_ledger\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\01\a2T3 (2026-08-24): `Some(claim_id)` while a `submit_claim` for this\0awallet is sitting in `ClaimStatus::Reserved` (rejected for\0a`DailyStressCapExceeded`/`Insolvent`, not yet released or expired).\0aDeliberately separate from `active_claim_id`: a Reserved claim\0aisn't \22active\22 (it holds no capacity reservation: `total_allocated`\0ais untouched until release), but the wallet still can't queue a\0asecond one without this guard.\00\00\00\00\00\11reserved_claim_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10staked_at_ledger\00\00\00\04\00\00\01\01Real Unix timestamp at stake time, used ONLY for the absolute\0ahack_timestamp sanity check in submit_claim (\22hack can't predate\0athe stake\22). staked_at_ledger remains the source of truth for all\0aduration/gate math (time gate, cooldown, vesting, penalty lock).\00\00\00\00\00\00\13staked_at_timestamp\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00HAdmin can block payout eligibility; does NOT block principal withdrawal.\00\00\00\09suspended\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09withdrawn\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\08`YieldIndex` at the moment this stake was created. `withdraw()`\0acomputes the payout as `amount * current_index / yield_index_at_stake`.\0aThis is the snapshot half of that ratio, so a staker only accrues\0ayield realised AFTER they joined, never retroactively. Fresh stakes\0aon a pool that has never realised yield snapshot at\0a`YIELD_INDEX_PRECISION` (the 1.0x starting value), so the ratio is\0aexactly 1 until the first `extract_yield` call.\0a\0ar3 (2026-09-29): the index is ADDITIVE per unit of principal (each\0acredit adds `share * PRECISION / total_staked`), so yield owed is\0a`amount * (YieldIndex - yield_index_at_stake) / PRECISION`. The old\0aratio `amount * index / at_stake` underpaid anyone who joined after\0athe first credit. Reset to the live index whenever yield is paid out.\00\00\00\14yield_index_at_stake\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cBackerRecord\00\00\00\07\00\00\00<Matured money: counts toward capacity, can be requested out.\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00DDeposited but not yet matured: held, does NOT count toward capacity.\00\00\00\0epending_amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00DTimestamp at which `pending_amount` matures; 0 when nothing pending.\00\00\00\12pending_matures_at\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00[Open withdrawal request (0 = none). Still counted toward capacity\0auntil completed (rule 2).\00\00\00\00\0fwithdraw_amount\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\003Earliest completion timestamp for the open request.\00\00\00\00\11withdraw_ready_at\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00=r3: `BackerYieldIndex` at the last settlement of this record.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eyield_index_at\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\002r3: yield settled to this backer and not yet paid.\00\00\00\00\00\0ayield_owed\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fOverrideRequest\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12co_signer_approver\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bentitlement\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\01\e7The actual approving address, not a bare bool, found via\0aadversarial review (2026-07-14, Solodit \22operator retains power\0aafter removal\22 pattern class): a bool can't tell a CURRENT\0aadmin/coSigner's approval apart from a STALE one left over from\0abefore a set_co_signer/transfer_admin rotation. Readiness is\0aderived by comparing these against the CURREN